# Leyline of Punishment begins the game on Bot1's battlefield: "Players can't gain life." A replacement effect that would
# replace a life gain event affecting a player who can't gain life does nothing (CR 119.7). So when Bot1's Swords to
# Plowshares exiles Bot2's Healer's Hawk, Bot2 neither gains 1 life nor, through Tainted Remedy, loses it (20).

[Bot1 Deck]
Leyline of Punishment
Swamp
Sol Ring
Mox Jet
Tainted Remedy
Plains
Swords to Plowshares
Swamp x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Healer's Hawk
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tainted Remedy.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Healer's Hawk.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Healer's Hawk)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Leyline of Punishment.Types = Enchantment
Bot2.Life = 20
Exile = Healer's Hawk
